RandomFoodSpawnStrategy uses a 20% bonus probability, meaning food type is not deterministic. What does that make harder, and how does the project work around it?,Nothing - randomness has no effect on anything,"It makes runs non-reproducible, so the demos pass a seeded Random such as new Random(42) - producing the same sequence every time and making the printed output something you can actually assert against","It makes the game unfair, so the seed is used to remove randomness entirely",It prevents the strategy from being swapped at runtime,,2,Seeding is what let the recorded run be checked line by line. Randomness taken from an injected Random rather than a global one is what makes that possible.,2

