// From the PARKING LOT project (class-29)
public class SpotFactory {
    private static final Map<SpotSize, ISpot> strategies = new HashMap<>();

    static {
        strategies.put(SpotSize.COMPACT, new CompactSpot());
        ...
    }

    public ISpot getSpot(SpotSize spotSize) {
        return strategies.get(spotSize);
    }
}

The parking lot cached one pre-built object per kind and handed the same instance to every caller, which was a bug. The snake's creators build a new FoodItem on every call. Why is the difference correct in both directions?,The parking lot version was fine
